UPDATE "tones" SET "definition" = $positive$The author uses this appearance to present what the term refers to as good, worthy, or something to be sought or aspired to. Praise, credit, defense, hope, and a claim that it deserves something belong here. In "Africa deserves to decide its own future," Africa is used this way.$positive$ WHERE "name" = 'Positive' AND ("definition" IS NULL OR btrim("definition") = '');
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "tones" SET "definition" = $neutral$The author uses this appearance to mention what the term refers to without presenting it as good or bad. A fact, a definition, a name, or a description with no praise and no blame belongs here. In "Africa is one of Earth's continents," Africa is used this way.$neutral$ WHERE "name" = 'Neutral' AND ("definition" IS NULL OR btrim("definition") = '');
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "tones" SET "definition" = $negative$The author uses this appearance to present what the term refers to as bad, at fault, or something to be avoided or rejected. Blame, criticism, failure, threat, and a claim that it has fallen short belong here. In "Africa hasn't carried its weight in negotiations," Africa is used this way.$negative$ WHERE "name" = 'Negative' AND ("definition" IS NULL OR btrim("definition") = '');
